: "Opus 5.5 resigned as White against the 10k, so Black won B+R. Black led from the middle game on, and the analysis put Black at +72.1 when the game ended. Opus 5.5 averaged 8.0 points lost per move with 13 blunders, against 5.5 and 7 for the 10k. Both sides gave away huge swings in the corner fight around B7 and A8, and the game ended in resignation.", "moments": [{"turn": 14, "text": "H3 cost Opus 5.5 11.5 points and moved Black's lead from +3.3 to +14.8. The engine preferred D6, and Black kept the edge from here on."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "The 10k answered with H2, which lost 19.1 points and took Black's lead from +24.3 down to +5.2. It was the biggest chance Opus 5.5 got, and the engine's choice here was C6."}, {"turn": 44, "text": "B7 lost 45.4 points, the worst move of the game, and pushed Black's lead from +27.3 to +72.7. The engine wanted C2. Opus 5.5 kept playing on the left edge, but the numbers never came back near even."}, {"turn": 53, "text": "A8 lost 45.2 points for the 10k and cut Black's lead from +71.9 to +26.7. Before it, White had the ko-capturing stone on B5. After it, the White stones at A7, B7 and B8 were gone, and the engine's choice was C2."}, {"turn": 54, "text": "B4 lost 45.2 points and handed the lead straight back, from +26.7 to +71.9. The engine's choice was D2. With one move each side had undone the other's 45-point error, which left Black far ahead."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only flood-fills the pasted board to list groups and their liberties, count.py only tallies stones and enclosed empty regions for an area count, and the cat/tail/append of games.md just reads and writes notes; none of it enumerates candidate moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}